WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
MobaRust: servers, shells and files in one native workspace.

00:03.000 --> 00:13.000
Run a real local shell command and reach a disposable loopback HTTP service.

00:13.000 --> 00:23.000
Keep independent tasks side by side in two terminal panes.

00:23.000 --> 00:33.000
This authenticated SSH connection uses generated keys and explicit host trust.
Remote commands return real output from the disposable server.

00:33.000 --> 00:47.000
Browse remote SFTP files and edit a generated configuration in the app.
The editor checks remote changes before saving.

00:47.000 --> 00:52.000
The SFTP download completed. Its bytes match the generated source file.
The absolute local destination path is obscured.

00:52.000 --> 01:02.000
Create a local SSH forward with explicit bind and target fields.
Loopback is the default; port zero selects a free listener port.

01:02.000 --> 01:12.000
This curl request passes through the SSH tunnel to the loopback HTTP service.

01:12.000 --> 01:22.000
Save a snippet, supply its variable and review the rendered command.
Nothing runs automatically.

01:22.000 --> 01:30.000
Switch between dark and light themes. Terminal colors follow the workspace.

01:30.000 --> 01:34.000
Mac 0.1.17 preview; Windows/Linux 0.1.12. No publisher signing.
